{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25595340",
      "title": "What is React.js? And Why Would You Use It?",
      "sourceHash": "c8259fe7e1c32f98da439843abda975004cff9114bc48a51f1642f3863520700",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "So what is React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 5.94,
          "en": "and why exactly would you use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.94,
          "end": 9.36,
          "en": "Well, if we visit the official webpage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.36,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "react.dev, we get an answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "It's a library for web and native user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "So put in other words, React is a library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 22.83,
          "en": "for building user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.83,
          "end": 24.51,
          "en": "That's what React is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.51,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "And as it turns out, it's a JavaScript library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.29,
          "end": 30.51,
          "en": "for building user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 33.769,
          "en": "But that of course, still doesn't answer the other question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.769,
          "end": 36.15,
          "en": "Why would you use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.15,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "And the answer can be found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 40.446,
          "en": "if you visit a webpage that uses React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.446,
          "end": 43.02,
          "en": "like, for example, Netflix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.02,
          "end": 45.99,
          "en": "As you navigate around on such a website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.99,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "you'll see that all these transitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "are super smooth, pretty much instant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "and you never have this effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 56.97,
          "en": "where you seem to load a new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.97,
          "end": 59.82,
          "en": "So where you seem to wait for a new page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 62.01,
          "en": "to be sent back by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "To some extent, it therefore feels like a mobile app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 69.18,
          "en": "because in mobile apps, getting instant feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.18,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "and having smooth transitions is pretty much the standard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 76.38,
          "en": "And it's libraries like React that help us build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.38,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "such user experiences, such user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "for the web as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "Because React, since it's a JavaScript library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 89.78999999999999,
          "en": "uses JavaScript in the browser to update the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.78999999999999,
          "end": 92.71600000000001,
          "en": "and the user interface we see on that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.71600000000001,
          "end": 95.46000000000001,
          "en": "without reloading the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.46000000000001,
          "end": 97.56,
          "en": "JavaScript can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.56,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "because JavaScript in the end runs kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "of in the background of a website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "and JavaScript is able to read and manipulate the webpage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "after it was loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 110.164,
          "en": "So JavaScript can, for example, make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.164,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "that as I click on the movies tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.95,
          "en": "it fetches the movie's data behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 119.67,
          "en": "in the background without reloading or leaving the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.67,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "and it then updates what I see on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 124.08,
          "en": "with that movie's data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 127.62,
          "en": "leading to that smooth transition between those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.62,
          "end": 129.03,
          "en": "But wait a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 131.52,
          "en": "Since this is all JavaScript in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 135.6,
          "en": "why do we need this React library for JavaScript?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.6,
          "end": 138.36,
          "en": "Because as you'll see in the next lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 141.489,
          "en": "where I'll compare using just JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.489,
          "end": 144.673,
          "en": "to using libraries like React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.673,
          "end": 148.821,
          "en": "working with just JavaScript, of course, is an option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.821,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "but it isn't a great one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "It's cumbersome, it means more work for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 157.68,
          "en": "it can be more error-prone, and especially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.68,
          "end": 160.68,
          "en": "if you're building more complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.68,
          "end": 165.24,
          "en": "and more complex applications like this Netflix web app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.24,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "then using just vanilla JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "so without any library like React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.04,
          "en": "would just be a huge pain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.04,
          "end": 177.153,
          "en": "and wouldn't be a very realistic option, to be honest.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}